from (values
('127.721.d.2.C',3,'The student must choose between a live demo, a recorded video and a website for sharing results with a local business. The choice should be based on:','["coin flip", "the file size only", "what best reaches and informs the audience", "the color only"]'::jsonb,2,'Audience and purpose drive the method.','original'),
('127.721.d.2.C',4,'A research summary for a rural group without reliable internet is best published as:','["a website that requires fast service", "a live webinar only", "a streaming-only video", "a printable or downloadable report"]'::jsonb,3,'Match the method to access.','original'),
('127.721.d.2.D',3,'A student turns a research paper into a poster, a slide set and a web page. This is:','["synthesizing and publishing in print and digital formats", "hiding results", "copying others", "deleting the paper"]'::jsonb,0,'Multiple formats share the work.','original'),
('127.721.d.2.D',4,'Publishing information in several formats helps because:','["it hides the message", "different audiences prefer different media", "it needs no planning", "it lowers accuracy"]'::jsonb,1,'Variety broadens reach.','original'),
('127.721.d.2.E',3,'Two students in different cities build a shared prototype using an online whiteboard and cloud storage. They rely on:','["local-only files", "a typewriter", "evolving network resources to create and exchange work", "paper only"]'::jsonb,2,'Network tools enable distance collaboration.','original'),
('127.721.d.2.E',4,'Which network resource best supports exchanging large project files with a mentor?','["a paper letter", "a verbal description", "a sticky note", "a secure cloud folder"]'::jsonb,3,'Cloud storage shares large files.','original'),
('127.721.d.2.F',3,'A student exchanges design ideas with a technology class in another country and learns how they solve similar problems. This builds:','["cultural understanding and global awareness", "less knowledge", "confusion", "isolation"]'::jsonb,0,'Cross-cultural exchange builds awareness.','original'),
('127.721.d.2.F',4,'One benefit of working with learners from other cultures on technology projects is:','["identical answers", "seeing a wider range of approaches and needs", "less learning", "fewer ideas"]'::jsonb,1,'Diversity widens perspectives.','original'),
('127.721.d.2.G',3,'A team agrees on a problem statement, lists hypotheses and assigns who tests each one. They are:','["working alone", "skipping planning", "collaborating to identify a problem and strategies", "ignoring the problem"]'::jsonb,2,'Teams plan together.','original'),
('127.721.d.2.G',4,'A collaborative plan for solving a problem is stronger when each hypothesis has:','["no method", "no owner", "no timeline", "a defined strategy for testing it"]'::jsonb,3,'Hypotheses need test strategies.','original'),
('127.721.d.2.H',3,'A student answers other users'' questions on a coding forum and also asks for help when stuck. This is participating as:','["a learner and contributor in an electronic community", "an anonymous troll", "a silent observer only", "a spammer"]'::jsonb,0,'Active participation includes learning and giving.','original'),
('127.721.d.2.H',4,'The best behavior in an electronic community is to:','["hoard answers", "share accurate help and treat others respectfully", "post rudely", "mock beginners"]'::jsonb,1,'Respect and accuracy are key.','original'),
('127.721.d.2.I',3,'A student helps a nonprofit set up a simple website as part of the study. This is:','["a private hobby", "an exam", "a meaningful activity in the larger community", "a secret task"]'::jsonb,2,'Service links learning to community.','original'),
('127.721.d.2.I',4,'Community projects in an independent study help students to:','["limit growth", "avoid real life", "skip work", "apply technology skills to real needs"]'::jsonb,3,'Application deepens learning.','original'),
('127.721.d.3.A',3,'A student locates recent journals and shares findings with a mentor through a collaboration platform. This uses:','["network and Internet resources for research and sharing", "only paper", "only a library card", "only memory"]'::jsonb,0,'Networks aid research.','original'),
('127.721.d.3.A',4,'The most efficient way to share a research bibliography with a remote mentor is:','["a paper stack", "a shared online document", "a phone call only", "a handwritten note"]'::jsonb,1,'Shared documents are efficient.','original'),
('127.721.d.3.B',3,'To locate peer-reviewed studies, a student uses advanced search with keywords and date filters. This is:','["clicking randomly", "using only ads", "applying search strategies to acquire information", "ignoring results"]'::jsonb,2,'Targeted searching is efficient.','original'),
('127.721.d.3.B',4,'Adding a minus sign before a word in a search tells the engine to:','["print results", "ignore the whole search", "delete the page", "exclude results containing that word"]'::jsonb,3,'Operators narrow results.','original'),
('127.721.d.3.C',3,'A student asks, "Does a darker interface theme reduce eye strain in night use?" This is:','["a question tied to a selected problem", "a citation", "a conclusion", "a title page"]'::jsonb,0,'Questions drive research.','original'),
('127.721.d.3.C',4,'A well-formed hypothesis for the study must be:','["unprovable", "testable and related to the problem", "unrelated", "already proven"]'::jsonb,1,'Testability is essential.','original'),
('127.721.d.3.D',3,'For each fact in her report, Dana records where it came from. She is:','["copying", "guessing", "acquiring information with source citations", "hiding sources"]'::jsonb,2,'Source records support credibility.','original'),
('127.721.d.3.D',4,'Including accurate citations in a research product shows the student:','["avoided research", "has no sources", "copied everything", "respects the work of other authors"]'::jsonb,3,'Citing gives credit.','original'),
('127.721.d.3.E',3,'A student creates a podcast, a slideshow, a spreadsheet and a PDF for one project. These show use of:','["a variety of file formats", "no formats", "a single format", "only text"]'::jsonb,0,'Projects often use many formats.','original'),
('127.721.d.3.E',4,'When choosing a format for a report to be read on any device, the best option is a:','["hidden format", "widely supported, cross-platform format", "corrupted file", "rare proprietary format"]'::jsonb,1,'Common formats open anywhere.','original'),
('127.721.d.4.A',3,'Before citing a statistic, a student confirms the publisher''s reputation and checks whether other reliable sources agree. This is:','["ignoring errors", "skipping checks", "evaluating the accuracy of accessed information", "accepting any claim"]'::jsonb,2,'Accuracy requires verification.','original'),
('127.721.d.4.A',4,'A claim appears on one anonymous blog and nowhere else. The student should:','["cite it as fact", "copy it", "ignore all other sources", "treat it with caution and look for corroboration"]'::jsonb,3,'Corroborate uncertain claims.','original'),
('127.721.d.4.B',3,'A student sets research questions, searches multiple databases, compares results and records the process. This is:','["conducting systematic research", "random browsing", "guessing", "skipping documentation"]'::jsonb,0,'Systematic research is planned and recorded.','original'),
('127.721.d.4.B',4,'The main value of recording search terms and databases used is that it:','["removes accuracy", "lets others repeat and verify the research", "wastes time", "hides the method"]'::jsonb,1,'Records support verification.','original'),
('127.721.d.4.C',3,'Faced with a failed prototype, Lena sketches three alternative designs and tests each. She is showing:','["avoidance", "copying", "creative thinking and problem-solving skills", "quitting"]'::jsonb,2,'Exploring alternatives builds solutions.','original'),
('127.721.d.4.C',4,'A creative problem solver whose approach fails tends to:','["blame tools", "give up", "repeat the same step", "analyze why and try a different approach"]'::jsonb,3,'Analysis and adaptation are central.','original'),
('127.721.d.4.D',3,'A student gathers field data on a tablet that syncs to a shared spreadsheet and a project board. This integrates:','["network, mobile access and productivity tools", "unrelated tools", "only paper tools", "no tools"]'::jsonb,0,'Integrated tools streamline work.','original'),
('127.721.d.4.D',4,'Which setup best integrates mobile access with productivity tools for team data entry?','["A paper log", "A phone form that writes to a shared spreadsheet", "A voicemail", "A printed chart"]'::jsonb,1,'Mobile forms feed shared files.','original'),
('127.721.d.4.E',3,'A student includes real statistics from a math unit and diagrams from science in the study''s final product. This is:','["avoiding content", "ignoring data", "using enriched curricular content in creating products", "using blank charts"]'::jsonb,2,'Cross-curricular content enriches products.','original'),
('127.721.d.4.E',4,'Using accurate content from other classes in a technology product helps by:','["making it empty", "hiding the topic", "lowering quality", "making the product more informative and credible"]'::jsonb,3,'Content adds depth.','original'),
('127.721.d.4.F',3,'From several electronic surveys, a student builds one new data set and writes new insights. This is:','["synthesizing and generating new information from gathered data", "deleting data", "hiding results", "copying one survey"]'::jsonb,0,'Synthesis produces new insight.','original'),
('127.721.d.4.F',4,'True synthesis of electronic data requires:','["summarizing nothing", "combining sources and drawing original conclusions", "skipping analysis", "repeating one source"]'::jsonb,1,'New information comes from combining data.','original'),
('127.721.d.4.G',3,'To configure a router, a student follows the manufacturer''s setup guide step by step. This is:','["skipping steps", "guessing", "reading and using technical documentation", "ignoring directions"]'::jsonb,2,'Technical manuals guide tasks.','original'),
('127.721.d.4.G',4,'A good habit when using technical documentation is to:','["skip the warnings", "ignore diagrams", "read only the index", "read warnings and notes before starting the steps"]'::jsonb,3,'Warnings prevent mistakes.','original'),
('127.721.d.4.H',3,'A student drafts a short how-to for new users of her project app, written at a beginner level. This is:','["simple technical documentation written for the audience", "a private note", "a cartoon", "a poem"]'::jsonb,0,'Write for the reader.','original'),
('127.721.d.4.H',4,'Technical documentation for non-experts should include:','["no instructions", "plain steps and examples", "only diagrams without labels", "unexplained jargon"]'::jsonb,1,'Clarity serves the audience.','original'),
('127.721.d.5.A',3,'A class discussion covers why reposting a stranger''s artwork without permission may violate copyright and why sharing someone''s private data can harm them. The topics are:','["cable colors", "font styles", "intellectual property, privacy and information sharing", "paper sizes"]'::jsonb,2,'IP and privacy are core ethics topics.','original'),
('127.721.d.5.A',4,'Which is a privacy concern when posting online?','["Setting the volume", "Picking a font", "Choosing a page title", "Revealing someone''s address or photos without consent"]'::jsonb,3,'Privacy requires consent.','original'),
('127.721.d.5.B',3,'Sam obtains permission before using a dataset and lists the owner in the credits. This models:','["ethical acquisition and use of digital information", "spam", "piracy", "hacking"]'::jsonb,0,'Permission and credit are ethical practices.','original'),
('127.721.d.5.B',4,'A student who downloads a licensed image for free from the official site''s free section and credits the author is:','["stealing", "using digital information ethically", "plagiarizing", "hacking"]'::jsonb,1,'Use of free-licensed content with credit is ethical.','original'),
('127.721.d.5.C',3,'A video editor uses only clips whose license allows remixing and adds credits. This shows:','["avoiding credit", "copying", "respect for intellectual property when editing media", "disrespect for rights"]'::jsonb,2,'Respect rights and credit creators.','original'),
('127.721.d.5.C',4,'Before changing a copyrighted audio track for a project, a student should:','["hide the source", "assume it''s free", "remove the credit", "confirm the license allows modification"]'::jsonb,3,'Check license terms.','original'),
('127.721.d.5.D',3,'A student follows the lab''s acceptable-use rules, avoids unlicensed software and treats shared devices carefully. This is:','["responsible use of software and etiquette", "a data leak", "a policy breach", "reckless behavior"]'::jsonb,0,'Responsible use follows the rules.','original'),
('127.721.d.5.D',4,'A student who understands acceptable-use policies is more likely to:','["share passwords", "avoid actions that could cause harm or lose access", "damage equipment", "break rules"]'::jsonb,1,'Policy knowledge prevents problems.','original'),
('127.721.d.5.E',3,'Regularly updating software and using a password manager are:','["risky shortcuts", "bad habits", "information security best practices", "wasted effort"]'::jsonb,2,'Updates and managers protect data.','original'),
('127.721.d.5.E',4,'A phishing email tries to trick the user into revealing a login. Best practice is to:','["reply with the password", "forward to friends", "click quickly", "avoid clicking and report the message"]'::jsonb,3,'Reporting prevents harm.','original'),
('127.721.d.5.F',3,'A student stores manuals, setup guides and notes for every tool used in the project in an organized library. This is:','["developing and maintaining a technical documentation library", "hiding references", "deleting files", "losing notes"]'::jsonb,0,'Libraries support reuse.','original'),
('127.721.d.5.F',4,'Keeping documents in a library with clear names and categories means the student can:','["never find anything", "find reference material quickly later", "waste space", "avoid documentation"]'::jsonb,1,'Organization saves time.','original'),
('127.721.d.5.G',3,'A report examines how automation changed jobs and what ethical questions it raised. It investigates:','["hardware prices", "cable colors", "technology''s social and ethical ramifications", "screen sizes"]'::jsonb,2,'Technology reshapes society.','original'),
('127.721.d.5.G',4,'A social effect of facial recognition technology is:','["less data", "fewer cameras", "no effect", "debate over privacy and fairness"]'::jsonb,3,'New tech raises ethical issues.','original'),
('127.721.d.6.A',3,'A student correctly operates a scanner, tablet and stylus, and organizes files within the OS. This demonstrates:','["appropriate use of input devices and operating systems", "no skill", "avoiding the computer", "guessing"]'::jsonb,0,'Technical skills underpin the study.','original')
